#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08427311-55df-5fca-8c81-b3d43755834b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235853} {:answer/id #uuid "2353948c-bc8b-5f0b-98ab-1abe270ac07d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236042} {:answer/id #uuid "a4476340-bf39-5aaf-a573-7229498e24af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236846} {:answer/id #uuid "b7773c7d-3bdb-5acf-be2b-51eef75585ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236982} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd62949-9c60-508b-903d-59d06baacfbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08427311-55df-5fca-8c81-b3d43755834b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235853} :answer-field/id #uuid "83dde5d1-ffc2-549e-a497-8373df71d13d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98689422-75b7-52ec-a8b8-4a4a4c165a7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102674" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n\nII. $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n\nIII. $B={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $B={A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -5 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203d12f3-8c3a-5557-837d-97614900aecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250827} {:answer/id #uuid "37fa1324-7dc6-58cd-a405-664a3029c979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251017} {:answer/id #uuid "43c9ad1f-5027-564e-8d6f-f65d7b6af604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251120} {:answer/id #uuid "7d5992ac-076a-5473-a6d9-3e4bba83cb3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251599} {:answer/id #uuid "b34057e3-6fe3-51a0-8d42-660e355aaf1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b34057e3-6fe3-51a0-8d42-660e355aaf1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252122} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c14b9f0-5ae4-545c-9581-c501daf9503a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "297364cd-4444-5a41-ba36-21b226267ecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-11637" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $CD=DC={I}_{2}$\n\nII. $DE=ED={I}_{2}$\n\nIII. $D={C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0598c7f4-28a9-513b-9652-c49128eb7398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272440} {:answer/id #uuid "1c149f30-6edb-589b-a895-c63a6c10be77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272629} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2d4f85-3626-51a3-ab27-a8decea5dd92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274143} {:answer/id #uuid "d116eac8-d2a2-5632-8c9e-1d6fa4d60296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274208} {:answer/id #uuid "e20ce21d-b427-5776-bf6f-a1524e79e261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c149f30-6edb-589b-a895-c63a6c10be77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272629} :answer-field/id #uuid "a29be6bf-0589-5604-8bb6-15bf9652dfc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bdbd7939-21af-5d98-9fc2-2a05d548f266" :question/math-academy-id "q-149832" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n\nII. $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n\nIII. $B={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43339e1d-1bfa-55d0-b3c2-c8e4ad7e48be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336667} {:answer/id #uuid "7483dbfb-2a05-5002-b015-71ac4bbb50b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337079} {:answer/id #uuid "9bc56d9f-7969-5603-8164-402febf66e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337442} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a235c2-3d22-5e37-8f24-ef0a23a374c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337626} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0d9494-e399-55f1-8b32-0a285f986f3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2a235c2-3d22-5e37-8f24-ef0a23a374c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337626} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b488541-8354-522a-b07d-347ec327f286" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8aec4565-777c-5fd0-95ff-9f5ced653b55" :question/math-academy-id "q-71879" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $AB=BA={I}_{3}$\n\nII. $BC=CB={I}_{3}$\n\nIII. $A={B}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $A\\ne {B}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}]}
